  --external:@/*`.
- OpenSpec strict validation passed:
  `/tmp/tl315-openspec-cli/node_modules/.bin/openspec validate fix-arm64-build-duplicate-declarations --strict --no-interactive`.

An isolated `npm ci` installed dependencies in the task worktree with
`PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_BROWSER_DOWNLOAD=1`; generated dependencies and build
artifacts were removed afterward. `npm run build:contributor` reached Next.js
16.3.8 webpack compilation in backend-only mode, then exited with SIGTERM after
about 15 minutes before reporting a result. No duplicate-binding diagnostic
appeared before termination, but this is inconclusive, not a passing build.
`npm run check:open-sse-typecheck` reported seven diagnostics in unchanged
files; none were TS2300 diagnostics in the repaired modules. The focused
TypeScript binder test proves the two reported duplicate-binding failures are
gone. esbuild bundle checks cover syntax in the resolved local import graphs,
not complete Next.js webpack behavior or ARM64 image acceptance. No task-owned
app build process remains; do not retry local builds under the current host
rule. No workflow dispatch, image build, publish, or deploy occurred.
